77:**Amendments during implementation (logged in the notebook):** (A1, 2026-09-12 15:1x) the empirical-uniformity test uses a chi-square sanity bound (χ² < 700 over 512 bins, 511 d.o.f.) instead of a ±5 % per-bin rule, which rejects a correct generator at 10^6 draws. (A2, same time) `rotate_scene_yaw_batch` is implemented in `tools/yaw_aug.py`, not in `tools/yaw_rotation.py`, which stays byte-identical to exp_03's reviewed state so exp_03's committed closure pins remain valid; the exp_04 training closure therefore contains the unchanged `tools/yaw_rotation.py` plus `tools/yaw_aug.py` (the §5 table's first row is read with this relocation). (A3, 2026-09-12 16:0x) The same rule applies to every member of exp_03's pinned closure, in particular `eval_yaw_rotation.py`: the evaluation-manifest handshake, the `--conditions P` mode and the tier/provenance metadata of §4/§5 are implemented in a NEW entry point `tools/exp04_eval.py` that imports `eval_yaw_rotation`'s functions unchanged (same outputs for the same inputs, tested on a 32-query subset), and `eval_yaw_rotation.py` is not edited; the §5 row "`eval_yaw_rotation.py`" is read as "`tools/exp04_eval.py`". (A4, same time) The trainer's counter uses `batches_per_epoch = len(train_loader)` (recorded in `args.json`, injectivity `epochs × batches_per_epoch < 2^20` asserted); the confirmatory run's launcher asserts `batches_per_epoch == 9261`, so the registered counter `t = (epoch−1)·9261 + batch_idx` holds for the reported run while smokes with other loader lengths remain possible. §2's counter sentence and the banner are read as `t = (epoch−1)·B + batch_idx`, `B = len(train_loader)` (banner `counter=(epoch-1)*<B>+batch_idx`; B = 9261 for the confirmatory run). (A5, 2026-09-12 16:3x, from the Fable round-2 review, finding 3) The trainer's `args.json` now carries `train_batches_per_epoch` and `env`, which the exp_01 control's `args.json` lacks; the §2 type-strict `effective_args` diff compares `train_batches_per_epoch` against the value reconstructed for the control by the same loader arithmetic (ceil(296334/32) = 9261) and treats `env` as the schema's environment block (control values reconstructed from the exp_01 record; `PYTHONHASHSEED` excluded as already specified). (A6, 2026-09-12 18:4x, from the Fable round-3b review, finding 2) `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` is excluded from the control-parity diff: the device index is not a recipe parameter (both cards are identical RTX A6000s; exp_01's control trained on GPU 1), and the treatment trains on whichever card the launcher is given (`--gpu`), recorded in `effective_args.json`; §5/§7's `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` is read as `<gpu>`. (A7, same time, finding 3) Finalisation policy: after the child exits the launcher re-hashes the genuinely mutable inputs strictly (`effective_args.json`, `train_manifest.json`, the control's `args.json`, the bound probe receipt, the training-split inventory) but compares the source closures against the immutable `reviewed_blob_sha256` recorded at spawn; working-tree drift of closure files after spawn cannot affect the running interpreter and is recorded in `completion.json` as `source_drift_after_spawn` instead of aborting; a `finalize <attempt_dir>` mode re-runs output validation → revalidation → completion → promotion for a preserved attempt once the child's process group is gone and the log sink is closed. (A8, same time, finding 10) The 43 h cumulative ceiling of §7 counts `full` attempts only; smoke and probe attempts are recorded in `cumulative_hours.json` with their mode but not summed. (A9, 2026-09-12 19:0x, from the Coder's round-4 report) The approved closure digests (evaluator, manifest writer, launchers, producers) are NOT stored inside `tools/exp04_profiles.py` — the producers import that module, so its own digest would be circular — but in a committed, runtime-read JSON `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_results_assets/approved_digests.json` (not imported, hence outside every import-derived closure); every producer records that file's sha256 and git blob in its provenance sidecar, the profiles keep every other field, and the second reviewed commit fills the JSON. Schema (settled 2026-09-12 19:2x after the Fable round-4 review): `{schema_version, closures: {evaluator, writer, training_launcher, producer_paired_compare, producer_results_table}, checkpoints: {aug: {path, epoch, sha256}}}`; the producers compare `evaluator`, `writer` and their own producer key only — the training launcher's identity reaches the analysis through the augmented checkpoint's sha256 and the train completion bound as `mutable_inputs.train_completion`, so `training_launcher` is recorded, not compared; the augmented checkpoint's sha256 lives in the JSON (not in the profile module) so that the producer closures are independent of the pin. Fill sequence after training: pin the aug sha256 → compute the producer closures → fill the JSON → second reviewed commit. `--exploratory` may run with unapproved pins, each recorded as a listed deviation (diagnostics only; no verdict). (A10, 2026-09-12 19:3x, from the Fable round-3b close-out review, finding 4) An attempt certified by `finalize` after an abort is renamed back to `attempt_<ts>` on success, its abort history (`abort.json`, the `_ABORTED_<reason>` name it carried, recovery timestamp) is recorded in `completion.json` under `recovered_from`, and `final` never points at an `_ABORTED_` directory. (Extension, 2026-09-12 22:3x, round 7: the attempt's log is renamed back alongside the directory; `recovered_from.log` records the aborted log name and `completion.log.path` the canonical one.)

